---
layout: none
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The search index. One entry per searchable page, built by Liquid at build
  time — no plugin, no Node step, nothing GitHub Pages cannot run.

  Body text is indexed, not just titles. On this site that is the whole point:
  a reader searches for "Drools", "template method" or "quality scenario", and
  those words live in section 8 of an example, never in a page title. That is
  also why this site uses lunr for the masthead suggestions where arc42.de
  uses a lighter title-only scorer — its titles are meaningful on their own,
  and these are not.

  `system` and `section` let a hit say WHERE it is: "MaMa-CRM · 3. Context and
  Scope" rather than a bare "Context and Scope", which is the same title in
  every example.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign landings = site.systems | where_exp: 'd', 'd.tagline' -%}
[
{%- assign sep = '' -%}

{%- for doc in site.systems -%}
  {%- assign slug = doc.path | remove_first: '_systems/' | split: '/' | first -%}
  {%- assign sys_url = '/systems/' | append: slug | append: '/' -%}
  {%- assign sys = landings | where: 'url', sys_url | first -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No system landing page means the directory is a template or is broken; it
    is not something a reader can be sent to.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if sys and doc.title -%}
{{ sep }}{
  "url": {{ doc.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "title": {{ doc.title | jsonify }},
  "system": {{ sys.title | jsonify }},
  "section": {{ doc.order | jsonify }},
  "content": {{ doc.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
}
    {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for page in site.pages -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Real pages only: search.json itself, 404, robots.txt and the sitemap carry
    either no title or nothing a reader wants to land on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if page.title and page.url != '/404.html' and page.search != false -%}
{{ sep }}{
  "url": {{ page.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "title": {{ page.title | jsonify }},
  "system": null,
  "section": null,
  "content": {{ page.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
}
    {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
